WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.342 --> 00:00:02.359
(somber music)

00:00:02.359 --> 00:00:04.188
- Being a transgender person,

00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:07.846
we battle so many fights
on our own inside.

00:00:07.846 --> 00:00:10.339
And when you can conquer that
and be your authentic self,

00:00:10.339 --> 00:00:13.756
there is nothing you can't fight and win.

00:00:18.343 --> 00:00:22.570
I enlisted in the military
because my family came to America

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.559
as refugees from Iran.

00:00:24.559 --> 00:00:26.205
And I wanted to give back to this country.

00:00:26.205 --> 00:00:28.384
It feels so good, because
you're doing something

00:00:28.384 --> 00:00:29.987
so much bigger than yourself.

00:00:29.987 --> 00:00:33.230
I was assigned to a
unit here in California.

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:37.621
And they just totally
swarmed me with compassion,

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:40.822
but I felt a little scared at the time,

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:42.845
because I was a lesbian.

00:00:42.845 --> 00:00:45.024
And I was scared that
people were going to know,

00:00:45.024 --> 00:00:45.949
and how they were going to treat me,

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:48.100
because, ""Don't ask, don't
tell" had just been repealed.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.815
I new that I was trans.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:51.942
And I'm going to be really
cliche and say my entire life.

00:00:51.942 --> 00:00:53.813
My experience transitioning

00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:56.444
while in military has been
a really interesting one.

00:00:56.444 --> 00:00:59.300
I started my hormone replacement
therapy when I was 23,

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.511
and that was about four years ago.

00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:01.647
I went and I sat down,

00:01:01.647 --> 00:01:03.039
and had a conversation with my commander.

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:04.762
And I was prepared to be discharged.

00:01:04.762 --> 00:01:05.645
I was really, really emotional,

00:01:05.645 --> 00:01:07.681
because I worked so hard
to be in the military.

00:01:07.681 --> 00:01:09.136
I didn't want to just get kicked out.

00:01:09.136 --> 00:01:11.266
And he pulls out this
counseling statement.

00:01:11.266 --> 00:01:15.156
Just that I needed to keep up
with male grooming standards.

00:01:15.156 --> 00:01:16.247
I just started crying,

00:01:16.247 --> 00:01:18.069
because I was thinking I
was going to get kicked out.

00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:20.193
And here I am having this
amazing chain of command

00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:21.523
that was just so supportive.

00:01:21.523 --> 00:01:22.439
For a lot of people in the military,

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:24.619
I was the first trans person
that they had ever met.

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:26.393
It was really awesome
to be able to sit down

00:01:26.393 --> 00:01:28.050
and explain to them what was happening

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.571
and who I am and how I felt.

00:01:29.571 --> 00:01:31.992
At the end of the day,
when we got our missions,

00:01:31.992 --> 00:01:33.025
we put our minds together,

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:36.085
and we focused on what
needed to be done, done.

00:01:36.085 --> 00:01:36.918
And that was it.

00:01:36.918 --> 00:01:39.931
I do not think being transgender
affects somebody's ability

00:01:39.931 --> 00:01:42.386
to be in the military and
to serve this country,

00:01:42.386 --> 00:01:43.749
honorably and courageously.

00:01:43.749 --> 00:01:44.582
As a matter of fact,

00:01:44.582 --> 00:01:46.722
I think being transgender
is a positive thing

00:01:46.722 --> 00:01:48.681
for the military, and for
this country as a whole.

00:01:48.681 --> 00:01:51.704
Cisgender people, and allies,
and other transgender people,

00:01:51.704 --> 00:01:54.437
what they can do to support
trans service members is

00:01:54.437 --> 00:01:55.967
continue to talk about us.

00:01:55.967 --> 00:01:58.544
Continue to talk about how great we are,

00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:01.372
and how important we are
in strength and compassion

00:02:01.372 --> 00:02:02.672
we bring to the military.

00:02:02.672 --> 00:02:04.425
So there are a lot of transgender people

00:02:04.425 --> 00:02:07.519
who have reached out to me on
social media and Instagram,

00:02:07.519 --> 00:02:11.555
that have expressed this really
intense interest and passion

00:02:11.555 --> 00:02:12.810
for wanting to serve in the military,

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.111
especially what's happening now.

00:02:14.111 --> 00:02:16.160
My advice to them is don't stop.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.791
If you want to serve in this military,

00:02:17.791 --> 00:02:18.741
go get enlisted.

00:02:18.741 --> 00:02:19.931
Go talk to a recruiter.

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:20.918
Be your authentic self.

00:02:20.918 --> 00:02:21.980
Don't hide anything.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.306
Don't lie, just be who you are,

00:02:24.306 --> 00:02:25.358
and serve this country.

00:02:25.358 --> 00:02:27.435
It's the one thing that I will always say,

00:02:27.435 --> 00:02:28.550
whether you're cisgender,

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.350
whether you're trans, gay, lesbian.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.474
It does not matter who you are.

00:02:31.474 --> 00:02:34.130
Never compromise your authenticity

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.790
for the comfort of others.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.957
(inspirational music)

